# Templates

- Keep templates simple — no business logic.
- Use **native control flow syntax** (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`) instead of `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`,
  `*ngSwitch`.
- Use the **async pipe** for observables.
- Use `[class]` and `[style]` bindings; avoid structural or dynamic directives like `ngClass`,
  `ngStyle`.
- **Never call methods in bindings** — precompute values in signals or computed.
- Use **Custom CSS** only.
- Prefer declarative markup; avoid structural complexity.
